				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"></span><table width="90%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="3" border="0" align="center"><tr> 	  <td><span class="genmed"><b>Quote:</b></span></td>	</tr>	<tr>	  <td class="quote">OK, 
<br />

<br />
Im getting real sick of all this... 
<br />

<br />
Ok first of all if the Sturmbot site is redirecting to the shrikebot site, how did this happen? Its not as if any of us here on the shrikebot team are hackers... And if you have no way to stop this from redirecting, dont you think it is time for you to get new domain name... I mean the only person who couldve changed this is Phuzzy himself.. correct? So the real question is.. what happened to phuzzy? Well maybe i can be of some assistance in answering this question... 
<br />

<br />
Myself and the other creator of shrikebot (Cpl_Shrike) were huge sturmbot fans back in the day (about 1 year ago) and still are.. at that time there was a post made, one that said Phuzzy had died.. With this post Shrike and I left the DoD comunity, and started our projects in tod... After about a month and a few beta releases.. A new but familiar name popped up in our forums, Mr (phuzzy) womble... He had made a post like this: 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
quote:
<br />
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />
Steve (err, Sarge), 
<br />

<br />
"Your handle is kinda spookie 'cause that's the handle a friend of mine used on ICQ before he passed away." &lt;-= 
<br />
"Least they only axed you and didnt kill your online presence (so to speak)." 
<br />

<br />
I went offline for two months due to setting my practice up and when I come back I got blasted by everyone I knew for calling myself Phuzzy. I couldnt even play on the Australian servers without someone biting a hole in my ass. 
<br />

<br />
It wasnt until I read the front page of the sturmbot site and the dod forums before I knew just what had gone down the last couple of months. 
<br />

<br />
The way I see things now, It's probably a good thing that they killed me off, I havent received any of the ever-so-annoying emails from sturmbotters, so I would prefer everyone who reads this keeps this news to themselves. 
<br />

<br />
Besides, anyone who used the sturmbot forum (pre-houston dod days) would know that I was 1000% against houston dod and would personally bitchslap Hogan back to WW2. 
<br />

<br />
It was bad enough my offline friends had trouble believing I was me. It wasnt until I showed up to one of their LANS they said "oh @#%$...". 
<br />

<br />
Was going to use the nick "The Ghost that walks" but Womble was a previous favourite of mine 
<br />

<br />
Finally, sturmbot wont be around forever. I've noticed the forum member numbers drop from 250-300 down to 70. What they didnt need was Hogan, afterall Sydslag is bad enough. 
<br />

<br />
I still own sturmbot.com so once shrikebot is all up and stable I may just route the domain to bring new people here 
<br />

<br />
Nowadays I'm into TOD (dod is going nowhere - 4.0 has brits... &lt;sarcasm&gt;wow&lt;/sarcasm&gt; ) and of course if you know me, you'd know i'm into BF1942. Although I've finished modelling vechicles for BF1942 still cant get the damn things in the game without them exploding on me. 
<br />

<br />
Once again, I'd appreciate those who read this letting Phuzzy (the nick) stay dead. 
<br />

<br />
Thanks, 
<br />
Womble 
<br />

<br />

<br />
Edited by: Womble at: 1/8/03 11:00:05 pm 
<br />
